csv:     table-10-hold-times.csv
source:  ../source.md
anchor:  TABLE X. Size and heat treatment of test coupons

# The source's own stated logic: the hold times are indexed by coupon diameter,
# and a thicker section cannot soak through in less time than a thinner one.
# So both time columns must be non-decreasing as diameter increases.  This is
# what catches a row shift between the diameter column and either time column
# -- the failure mode that put a 1-in coupon's 1-1/4 hr against a 3-in coupon.
monotonic:  coupon_diam_in increasing
monotonic:  austenitizing_hr non-decreasing
monotonic:  tempering_hr non-decreasing
